          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZATION_OF_PLAN_MESSAGES",
          "id": "1777635938673",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777635938675_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given structured data quality messages in JSON format. Summarize as Supply chain planners, who ensure that the input data provided on items and bill of materials is of good quality for reasonable planning results to review data quality messages, identify major errors, and resolve them immediately.\n\n## Input Data\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.topIssues}} \n\n## Critical Prioritization Rules\n### Severity Ranking (Highest Priority First)\n-Use message_severity as the primary prioritization criteria:\n1 = Critical\n2 = High\n3 = Medium\n4 = Low\n\n-Always prioritize:\n1. Lowest message_severity value first.\n2. If severities are equal, use highest message_count first.\n3. Never recommend a lower severity issue before a higher severity issue.\n\n## Parsing Rules\n-message_input_data is written as a string containing organization, items, resource, catalog, or other impacted planning entity variables.  \n-Sometimes the data is a pair of organization and item.  \n\tExample: Item Organization EKG-28 OR represents item EKG-28 in org OR.  \n-List items by the same organization instead of showing each pair separately.  \n\tExample 1: Item Organization EKG-28 OR ERG-32 OR EXG-28 RG EYG-37 RG EXJ-30 OR ETJ-23 OR represents items EKG-28, ERG-32, EXJ-30, and ETJ-23 in organization OR and items EXG-28 and EYG-37 in organization RG.  \n\tExample 2: Item Organization EKG-28 OR EXJ-30 OR EXG-28 RG represents items EKG-28 and EXJ-30 in org OR and item EXG-28 in org RG.\n\tExample 3: CategoryName CAT represents category CAT.  \n\tExample 4: LotName Item Organization ALK EKG-32 RG represents lot ALK for item EKG-32 in org RG.  \n-If ItemCount is provided, include the count of items.  \n\tExample: ItemCount Organization 1 RG represents a count of 1 item affected in org RG.\n-Below examples list possible messages and how it should be represented in the output.\n\tExample 1: SubInventory Organization Value SBJ RG YES PIJ RG YES represents subinventories SBJ and PIJ in organization RG.  \n\tExample 2: SubInventory Organization Value SBJ RG YES PIJ RG YES SKJ OR NO SBT OR YES represents subinventories SBJ and PIJ in organization RG and subinventories SKJ and SBT in organization OR.  \n\tExample 3: Item Organization Component EKG-32 OR PI-24-30 EKM-28 JR JP-31-26 ELM-87 JR JO-19-73 represents items and components EKG-32, PI-24-30, EKM-28, JP-31-26, ELM-87, JO-19-73 in organizations OR and JR.  \n\n## Rules\n- Do not reorder messages.\n- Group items by organization.\n- Do not output placeholder example values such as OR, RG, EKG-28, CAT, EKG-32, or ALK.\n- Do not put organization or item values in single quotes.\n\n## Task 1: Summary\n- Create a planner-focused summary.\n- Prioritize findings by severity (1 → 4).\n- Mention the most critical issues first.\n- Mention the most frequent issues using message_count.\n- Mention impacted items grouped by organization.\n- Limit to 7 sentences.\n- Do not use abbreviated message names.\n- Recommend one message to resolve first and explain planning impact.\n\n## Mandatory Step: Extract Impacted Entities\nFor each message:\n- Strictly adhere to Parsing Rules\n- You MUST extract items and organizations from message_input_data.\n- You MUST group items by organization.\n- You MUST explicitly include impacted items and their organizations in message_response.\n- If this step is skipped, the output is incorrect.\n\nExample:\nInput: Organization Item M1 A M1 B M1 C  \nOutput: items A, B, and C in organization M1\n\nDo not proceed to writing message_response until extraction is complete.\n## Task 2: Messages\n- Return ALL messages from input (do not skip any).\n- Keep original order.\n- For each message:\n  - Write exactly 3 sentences.\n  - Describe impacted items grouped by organization.\n  - Provide a clear resolution action.\nAlways reference extracted organizations, items, counts, resources, lots, categories, or subinventories.\n\n## IMPORTANT\n- You MUST return both \"summary\" and \"messages\".\n- \"messages\" array MUST include all input messages.\n- Do NOT stop after summary.\n- Output must be valid JSON.\n\n## Output\n{\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"description\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"message_name\": \"\",\n      \"message_short_text\": \"\",\n      \"message_count\": 0,\n      \"message_severity\": \"\",\n      \"message_response\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\n    \"summary\",\n    \"messages\"\n  ],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\n        \"description\"\n      ],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"description\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"messages\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\n          \"message_name\",\n          \"message_short_text\",\n          \"message_count\",\n          \"message_severity\",\n          \"message_response\"\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"message_name\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"message_short_text\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"message_count\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n          },\n          \"message_severity\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"message_response\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": false\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
